vtpm-mds for Proxmox / lab hosts
--------------------------------

This package installs only the daemon (/usr/sbin/vtpm-mds), the aliases
prox-mds and qemu-mds, the systemd unit, /etc/vtpm-mds/config.yaml and
/var/lib/vtpm-mds. The guest enrollment client is no longer part of it:
since 0.2.0 /usr/bin/devid-enroll lives in the separate devid-enroll
package, so upgrading vtpm-mds on a host removes that path. Install the
devid-enroll .deb in VM images (guests), not on the hypervisor.

This package does not configure the IMDS bridge, nftables DNAT, or
swtpm PKI — those typically come from site Ansible on the lab host:

  proxmox-imds-network  vmbr_imds 169.254.169.1/32 + DNAT 169.254.169.254:80
  proxmox-swtpm         EK/DevID CAs under /etc/ssl/certs and /etc/ssl/private

Default listen address is 169.254.169.1:80. Inventory is empty, so the
daemon parses /etc/pve. Packaged config.yaml points at:

  ek_ca_chain / attestation_ca  /etc/ssl/certs/proxmox_tpm_ca.crt
  devid_ca_cert                 /etc/ssl/certs/proxmox_devid_ca.crt
  devid_ca_key                  /etc/ssl/private/proxmox_devid_ca.key

If the Ansible role uses a different key suffix (e.g. .pem), edit the
conffile. Missing CA files disable DevID routes but IMDS still starts.

The unit is enabled on install but not started (so dpkg -i succeeds on
hosts without vmbr_imds). On the lab host:

  systemctl start vtpm-mds
  systemctl status vtpm-mds
  curl -sS http://169.254.169.1/health

Build
-----

One source builds both packages at the same version:

  make deb
  # artifacts: dist/vtpm-mds_<version>_<arch>.deb       (host daemon)
  #            dist/devid-enroll_<version>_<arch>.deb   (guest client)

Requires Go 1.24+ on PATH (go.mod toolchain) and debhelper. Equivalent:

  dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
  # writes the .debs to the parent of the source tree when that directory
  # is writable; `make deb` always stages into dist/.

Install the host package on the hypervisor, the guest package in the VM
image:

  sudo dpkg -i dist/vtpm-mds_*.deb && sudo systemctl start vtpm-mds
  sudo dpkg -i dist/devid-enroll_*.deb   # guest only; no service

GitHub Release (Linux amd64 only; tag v<changelog-version>). Both .debs
are attached to the same tag:

  gh release download v0.2.0 --repo dembaca/vtpm-mds --pattern 'vtpm-mds_*_amd64.deb'
  gh release download v0.2.0 --repo dembaca/vtpm-mds --pattern 'devid-enroll_*_amd64.deb'
  # https://github.com/dembaca/vtpm-mds/releases/download/v0.2.0/vtpm-mds_0.2.0_amd64.deb
  # https://github.com/dembaca/vtpm-mds/releases/download/v0.2.0/devid-enroll_0.2.0_amd64.deb
